    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:7c971c95bcc01fc5",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "aab0f7e69116bd544884ba590a2f033ce3fd13165850d40f21db6ce82a11acd3",
      "text": "The tour of the Brazilian side of the falls takes about **3 hours**.\n\nThe name Iguaçu comes from Guaraní and means “big water”. The falls comprise **275 cascades** on the border between Brazil and Argentina. One of the main sights is the Devil’s Throat.\n\nThe walking trails cover about **1,200 m** and lead to several panoramic viewpoints. As you near the end of the trail, the roar grows louder and you feel more of the spray.\n\n**Iguaçu Falls tour in Brazil — Macuco Safari**\n\nAfter the main walk, the itinerary continues with the **Macuco Safari**, which takes about **1 hour**.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
